#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:5
msgid "Public pages and registration"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:7
msgid "Galette can show a few pages to people who are not logged in, or to all your members: a list of members, a gallery of their pictures, the list of the staff, the public documents of the association. It can also let new people fill in a registration form themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:9
msgid "All of this is optional, and set from **Configuration**, then **Settings**."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:12
msgid "Public pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:14
msgid "The public pages are listed in the **Public pages** menu, or at the top of the login page for visitors."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:16
msgid "Public members list"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:21
msgid "**Members** and **Gallery**: the members of your association, as a list or with their pictures,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:22
msgid "**Staff** and **Staff gallery**: the members of the board only,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:23
msgid "**Documents**: the :ref:`documents <documents>` your association chose to share."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:25
msgid "Public members gallery"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:31
msgid "Who is listed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:33
msgid "A member only appears on the public lists of members when **all** the following conditions are met:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:35
msgid "they checked **Be visible on public pages:** on their member card,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:36
msgid "their account is active,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:37
msgid "their membership is up to date, or they are freed of dues."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:39
msgid "The staff lists show the members whose status makes them :ref:`staff members <man_generalites>`, if they agreed to be visible as well. The **Include groups managers with staff?** setting adds the group managers to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:41
msgid "Only some information is displayed: the name, the nickname, the picture, and the text of the **Other information** field of the member card."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:44
msgid "Who can see them?"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:46
msgid "In the **Parameters** tab of the settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:48
msgid "**Public pages enabled?** turns all public pages on or off,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:49
msgid "each page then has its own visibility:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:51
msgid "**Everyone**, including visitors who are not logged in,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:52
msgid "**Up to date members**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:53
msgid "**Admin and staff only**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:54
msgid "**Hidden**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:55
msgid "**Inherit**: the page follows the **Default** visibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:57
msgid "The **Default** visibility also applies to the public pages added by :doc:`plugins </plugins/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:61
msgid "Showing the list of your members to **Everyone** publishes their names on the Internet. Make sure your members agree, and that it complies with the rules on personal data that apply to your association."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:64
msgid "Self registration"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:66
msgid "When **Self registration enabled?** is checked in the **Parameters** tab of the settings, a **Register** button is displayed on the login page and on the public pages. Anyone can then fill in a form to become a member."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:68
msgid "Registration form"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:73
msgid "The form asks for the same information as the member form, and for a username and a password. A small question whose answer is a number, the *captcha*, has to be answered to prevent robots from registering."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:75
msgid "Once the form is sent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:77
msgid "the new member receives an email with their login information, if sending emails is configured,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:78
msgid "the administrators are informed by email, if **Send email to administrators?** is checked in the **E-Mail** tab of the settings,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:79
msgid "the new member gets the **Default membership status** set in the settings, and no contribution yet: it is up to the staff to check the request and record the membership fee."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:81
msgid "The emails that are sent can be changed from **Configuration**, then **Emails content**; see :ref:`emails contents <emails_contents>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/public_pages.rst:85
msgid "To limit abuse, a same address can only send a few registrations in a row: 5 per hour by default. Those limits can be changed from the :ref:`advanced configuration <advanced_config>`."
msgstr ""
